  "description": "M4A readability proof on the M1.5 micro_breach world (re-tagged as the m4a_micro_breach_readability scenario so the run bundle's metadata is source-truthful). Toggles all 9 ACC-A flags on at startup (ui_scale 2.0 + high_contrast + captions + reduced_motion + reduced_shake + reduced_flash + hold_to_confirm + hold_threshold_ms + key_remap_enabled), drives a focus-traversal cycle through every HUD node, then drives the player to: refused dig (out of range → tool_validity REFUSED) → walk into range → break the outer wall (terrain_carved) → cross into combat (actor_status_changed when the guard fires back) → reload (rifle module-strip transitions) → end on observe.once for accessibility evidence. Designed to exercise every M4A HUD line with non-default values.",
